class Solution {
    public int longestCommonSubsequence(String text1, String text2) {
        int n = text1.length();
        int m = text2.length();
        int[] prev = new int[m + 1];
        int[] curr = new int[m + 1];
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= m; j++) {
                if (text1.charAt(i - 1) == text2.charAt(j - 1)) {
                    curr[j] = 1 + prev[j - 1];
                } else {
                    curr[j] = Math.max(prev[j], curr[j - 1]);
                }
            }
            int[] temp = prev;                                                  // move current row to previous.
            prev = curr;
            curr = temp;
        }

        return prev[m];
    }
}
Space-O(n)


19)  // Longest Palindromic Substring. ->(Greedy/Two Pointer)

Every palindrome has a center and expands equally left & right.
class Solution {
    public String longestPalindrome(String s) {
        int start=0,end=0;
        for(int i=0;i<s.length();i++){
            int len1=expand(s,i,i+1);
            int len2=expand(s,i,i);
            int len=Math.max(len1,len2);
            if((end-start)<len){                                             // Center at i, Expand left by (len-1)/2, Expand right by len/2.
                start=i-(len-1)/2;
                end=i+len/2;
            }
        }
        return s.substring(start,end+1);
    }
    public int expand(String s,int i,int j){
        while(i>=0 && j<s.length() && s.charAt(i)==s.charAt(j)){
            i--;                                                         // keep expanding till boundary checks.
            j++;
        }
        return j-i-1;                                                                // return the length of the current palindrome.
    } 
}
Time-O(n^2)
Space-O(1)

More optimized approach is using Manachers algo.


