22)  // WildCard Matching.

1) Create dp[n+1][m+1].
2) Initialize base cases.
3) Loop through string and pattern.
4) Apply rules based on current pattern character.
5) Return dp[n][m].

class Solution {
    public boolean isMatch(String s, String p) {
        int n=s.length();
        int m=p.length();
        boolean[][] dp=new boolean[n+1][m+1];
        dp[0][0]=true;                                               // Empty pattern matches empty string.
        for(int j=1;j<=m;j++){                                       // Handle patterns like "*", "**", "***".
            if(p.charAt(j-1)=='*'){
                dp[0][j]=dp[0][j-1];
            }
        }
        for(int i=1;i<=n;i++){
         for(int j=1;j<=m;j++){                                                   // '*' can match empty or any sequence.
            if(p.charAt(j-1)=='?' || p.charAt(j-1)==s.charAt(i-1)){
                dp[i][j]=dp[i-1][j-1];
            }else if(p.charAt(j-1)=='*'){
                dp[i][j]=dp[i-1][j] || dp[i][j-1];
            }
         }
        }
        return dp[n][m];
   }
}
Time-O(n*m)
Space-O(n*m)


23)  // Egg Dropping Problem.

Case 1: Egg breaks -> You lose one egg. The critical floor is below it. -> Eggs left = k-1, Moves left = m-1, Floors you can test below = dp[k-1][m-1].
Case 2: Egg does NOT break -> Eggs remain same. The critical floow is above it.-> Eggs left = k, Moves left = m-1, Floors you can test above = dp[k][m-1].
class Solution {
    public int superEggDrop(int k, int n) {
        int[][] dp=new int[k+1][n+1];
        int mvs=0;
        while(dp[k][mvs]<n){
            mvs++;
            for(int eggs=1;eggs<=k;eggs++){
                dp[eggs][mvs]=1+dp[eggs-1][mvs-1]+dp[eggs][mvs-1];              // current floor + before + after.
            }
        }
        return mvs;
    }
}
Time-O(k*moves)
Space-O(k*moves)


24)  // Regular Expression Matching Problem.

class Solution {
    public boolean isMatch(String s, String p) {
        int n=s.length();
        int m=p.length();
        boolean[][] dp=new boolean[n+1][m+1];
        dp[0][0]=true;
        for(int j=1;j<=m;j++){
            if(p.charAt(j-1)=='*'){                                // in case the string is empty but pattern in non empty.
                dp[0][j]=dp[0][j-2];
            }
        }
        for(int i=1;i<=n;i++){
            for(int j=1;j<=m;j++){
               if(p.charAt(j-1)=='*'){                                      // here * means zero or more of preceding element.
                    dp[i][j]=dp[i][j-2];                                       // if i use it zero times then copy the j-2 value.
                    char prev=p.charAt(j-2);
                    if(prev=='.' || prev==s.charAt(i-1)){                   // so we check what is the preceding element.
                       dp[i][j]= dp[i][j] || dp[i-1][j];
                    }
                }
                else if(p.charAt(j-1)==s.charAt(i-1) || p.charAt(j-1)=='.'){
                    dp[i][j]=dp[i-1][j-1];                                          // copies the diagonal value if the characters are same or there is a '.'
            }
        }
    }
        return dp[n][m];
    }
}
Time-O(n*m)
Space-O(n*m)
NOTES-: one character consumed from string & one character consumed from pattern -> So we copy diagonal left (above) value.
        string stays same & pattern jumps -> So we copy left / j-2  cell value.(we are using x* 0 times).
        Pattern has * AND Current string character matches the character before * -> we take OR of the above cell value and itself.
